<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Transvaal Province</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1910">1910</a>–<a href="/years/1994">1994</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a> Province was one of the four provinces of the Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> and later the Republic, formed in 1910 from the Transvaal Colony, the former South African Republic. It contained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pretoria">Pretoria</a>, the administrative capital, and the gold-mining city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannesburg">Johannesburg</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/witwatersrand">Witwatersrand</a>. In 1994 it was divided into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gauteng">Gauteng</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mpumalanga">Mpumalanga</a>, the Northern Province, now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limpopo">Limpopo</a>, and part of North West.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/transvaal-province.jpg" alt="Transvaal Province" width="320" height="282" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Htonl · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Locator_map_of_Transvaal_Province_as_of_1_March_1994.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
